T*
([TECHNICAL GUIDE 1: SystemVerilog vs Verilog: Code Architecture Walkthrough]) Tj
T*
(Context: Illustrate why the semiconductor industry transitioned from Verilog to) Tj
T*
(SystemVerilog for verification.) Tj
T*
(Comparative Implementation Walkthrough:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Traditional Verilog-2001 \(Design Focus\): Primarily limited to static modules,) Tj
T*
(wire/reg types, and always blocks. Testbenches written in Verilog were static,) Tj
T*
(non-reusable, and could not generate constrained-random stimulus.) Tj
T*
(* 2. SystemVerilog OOP Verification Constructs: Introduces dynamic classes,) Tj
T*
(constrained randomization \(rand, constraint blocks\), functional coverage \(covergroup,) Tj
T*
